s1-p28 : Block
s1-p28 = prose (cons "**The language acts on its own constructions.** Grammars, judgments, interpretations, and transformations are represented definitions. A language's interpreter is an operand of the same activity as the expressions it interprets; transforming its represented clauses changes the interpretation of subsequent inputs (§6.3). Existing source languages retain their specified meaning while their definitions and programs become available to richer operations. Their syntax, interpretation, transformed source, and machine realization are related by the constructed evidence, not by separate semantic authorities." nil)
